+## Capability protocol v1 (message 16)
+
+After `SESSION_HELLO_ACK` on the authenticated/pinned session, the host sends
+`CAPABILITIES` (16), and the device replies once. Canonical CBOR payload keys:
+`version=1`, `session_id` (16 bytes, equal to hello), `endpoint` (`host` or
+`device`), `operations` (text array), `required` (text array). Arrays are at
+most 32 unique names, each at most 64 UTF-8 bytes. Unknown optional operation
+IDs are ignored. Unknown/missing required IDs, different session IDs, repeated
+changed advertisements and unsupported versions fail closed. No authentication
+request may be dispatched before an accepted device advertisement.
+
+Effective operations are the intersection of host-supported, device-supported,
+host-policy-enabled and device-policy-enabled operation IDs; the per-request
+biometric consent and account authorization must *also* succeed. Advertising
+capabilities never grants an authorization. Modifying negotiated capabilities
+requires a new authenticated session; no silent downgrade is supported.
